[{:db/id 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4e6f234b-737b-5376-aaeb-5d730bef9b84" "question-d152b171-fd28-5ce0-9099-77a199871a6f" "question-c4f686a5-889f-5e90-8c7e-36ce4fec4b92" "question-84ec701f-8d6f-546b-8f54-4258332a1413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d96a6265-af2d-5821-9fbc-e9e0d0216e3e" "question-a4a4a281-bd0c-502e-a09a-cc4e77ac53a7" "question-8e84a8d6-a1ed-5f78-832b-753ef57840b9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-941975f4-ea50-5edb-a299-e8568f71e188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4e6f234b-737b-5376-aaeb-5d730bef9b84" :question/id #uuid "4e6f234b-737b-5376-aaeb-5d730bef9b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-131742" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s={\\pi }^{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s={\\pi }^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}({\\pi }^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ({\\pi }^{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}({\\pi }^{2})‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\cdot \\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c322fadd-ac27-57ed-bf43-9e8ac0bbc8e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c322fadd-ac27-57ed-bf43-9e8ac0bbc8e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c322fadd-ac27-57ed-bf43-9e8ac0bbc8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba97ff6b-bf06-5c94-b2f1-739a2843f441" "answer-2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" "answer-cc70f6d3-c6fb-5244-881d-6bc189e3ab32" "answer-679116f9-97d1-5d62-a788-645a2d834296" "answer-12432056-a810-519c-9825-13b25ab2a228"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba97ff6b-bf06-5c94-b2f1-739a2843f441" :answer/id #uuid "ba97ff6b-bf06-5c94-b2f1-739a2843f441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" :answer/id #uuid "2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc70f6d3-c6fb-5244-881d-6bc189e3ab32" :answer/id #uuid "cc70f6d3-c6fb-5244-881d-6bc189e3ab32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-679116f9-97d1-5d62-a788-645a2d834296" :answer/id #uuid "679116f9-97d1-5d62-a788-645a2d834296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12432056-a810-519c-9825-13b25ab2a228" :answer/id #uuid "12432056-a810-519c-9825-13b25ab2a228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d152b171-fd28-5ce0-9099-77a199871a6f" :question/id #uuid "d152b171-fd28-5ce0-9099-77a199871a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131732" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=0$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨1,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d272c7ef-b48e-5924-96ef-203f6d488dc4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d272c7ef-b48e-5924-96ef-203f6d488dc4" :answer-field/id #uuid "d272c7ef-b48e-5924-96ef-203f6d488dc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8d6f9ca-3714-5aa5-8b78-a6f173247922" "answer-87f377ec-25a7-5af0-9e08-2729d14d17c3" "answer-a63b9eb5-9d48-5592-bb73-a581d4ffce7c" "answer-03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" "answer-55d8fe40-2fc5-5c9f-b218-ef946f9979e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8d6f9ca-3714-5aa5-8b78-a6f173247922" :answer/id #uuid "a8d6f9ca-3714-5aa5-8b78-a6f173247922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87f377ec-25a7-5af0-9e08-2729d14d17c3" :answer/id #uuid "87f377ec-25a7-5af0-9e08-2729d14d17c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a63b9eb5-9d48-5592-bb73-a581d4ffce7c" :answer/id #uuid "a63b9eb5-9d48-5592-bb73-a581d4ffce7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" :answer/id #uuid "03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55d8fe40-2fc5-5c9f-b218-ef946f9979e0" :answer/id #uuid "55d8fe40-2fc5-5c9f-b218-ef946f9979e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4f686a5-889f-5e90-8c7e-36ce4fec4b92" :question/id #uuid "c4f686a5-889f-5e90-8c7e-36ce4fec4b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-80521" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=2{\\pi }^{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=2{\\pi }^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\ {T}^{′}(2{\\pi }^{2}) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}{\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}{\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(2{\\pi }^{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(2{\\pi }^{2})‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2\\pi })}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70818e4d-0bd1-5756-b56e-538edbd5bffe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70818e4d-0bd1-5756-b56e-538edbd5bffe" :answer-field/id #uuid "70818e4d-0bd1-5756-b56e-538edbd5bffe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9a83a8d-c1c5-5b09-a81e-6dcef9136233" "answer-9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" "answer-2be96d5c-0914-5fe5-acba-da0c7e6d8b3a" "answer-5616aca8-3b97-5fdd-9cff-fae082d196cd" "answer-5562ffbc-ebce-5ef5-a7e7-e05b1cb533d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9a83a8d-c1c5-5b09-a81e-6dcef9136233" :answer/id #uuid "c9a83a8d-c1c5-5b09-a81e-6dcef9136233" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" :answer/id #uuid "9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2be96d5c-0914-5fe5-acba-da0c7e6d8b3a" :answer/id #uuid "2be96d5c-0914-5fe5-acba-da0c7e6d8b3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5616aca8-3b97-5fdd-9cff-fae082d196cd" :answer/id #uuid "5616aca8-3b97-5fdd-9cff-fae082d196cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5562ffbc-ebce-5ef5-a7e7-e05b1cb533d7" :answer/id #uuid "5562ffbc-ebce-5ef5-a7e7-e05b1cb533d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120494 :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119078 :answer-field/correct 17592186119080 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-84ec701f-8d6f-546b-8f54-4258332a1413" :question/id #uuid "84ec701f-8d6f-546b-8f54-4258332a1413" :question/math-academy-id "q-131743" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ \\\\  & =‖-\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e894091a-2e63-5373-8285-532c7e949b88"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e894091a-2e63-5373-8285-532c7e949b88" :answer-field/id #uuid "e894091a-2e63-5373-8285-532c7e949b88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" :answer-field/choices ["answer-206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" "answer-82909bce-1b68-5d11-be22-86b127324a90" "answer-e34cad78-7ce1-5b5b-aa1e-1145d9440cd7" "answer-bdc52b86-edc3-5ab3-8c53-46f3784df89f" "answer-38a62d49-ab80-5de1-b7d6-df3c195fadb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" :answer/id #uuid "206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82909bce-1b68-5d11-be22-86b127324a90" :answer/id #uuid "82909bce-1b68-5d11-be22-86b127324a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e34cad78-7ce1-5b5b-aa1e-1145d9440cd7" :answer/id #uuid "e34cad78-7ce1-5b5b-aa1e-1145d9440cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdc52b86-edc3-5ab3-8c53-46f3784df89f" :answer/id #uuid "bdc52b86-edc3-5ab3-8c53-46f3784df89f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38a62d49-ab80-5de1-b7d6-df3c195fadb0" :answer/id #uuid "38a62d49-ab80-5de1-b7d6-df3c195fadb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d96a6265-af2d-5821-9fbc-e9e0d0216e3e" :question/id #uuid "d96a6265-af2d-5821-9fbc-e9e0d0216e3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131945" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\frac{4}{5}s⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{5}s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\frac{4}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{3}{25}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92b6ebf7-c2b9-5972-b09e-a6f7847a9371"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92b6ebf7-c2b9-5972-b09e-a6f7847a9371" :answer-field/id #uuid "92b6ebf7-c2b9-5972-b09e-a6f7847a9371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6f59c1d-0707-55ca-b46e-a15a0d3ed556" "answer-5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" "answer-a2a2861c-388d-58fc-af3f-6ca10eb128d3" "answer-eda35170-2016-5f0d-84da-1b5c4583cefb" "answer-625782b0-4ad1-5de1-8987-e95b17c343ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6f59c1d-0707-55ca-b46e-a15a0d3ed556" :answer/id #uuid "f6f59c1d-0707-55ca-b46e-a15a0d3ed556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" :answer/id #uuid "5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2a2861c-388d-58fc-af3f-6ca10eb128d3" :answer/id #uuid "a2a2861c-388d-58fc-af3f-6ca10eb128d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eda35170-2016-5f0d-84da-1b5c4583cefb" :answer/id #uuid "eda35170-2016-5f0d-84da-1b5c4583cefb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-625782b0-4ad1-5de1-8987-e95b17c343ec" :answer/id #uuid "625782b0-4ad1-5de1-8987-e95b17c343ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120326 :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}},\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩,\\,0\\le s<2\\sqrt{10}\\,\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}},\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨1,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1),\\,-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨0,\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{0+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118095 :answer-field/correct 17592186118099 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-a4a4a281-bd0c-502e-a09a-cc4e77ac53a7" :question/id #uuid "a4a4a281-bd0c-502e-a09a-cc4e77ac53a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-83643" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where:\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{3-8s}{10},\\,\\frac{6s+4}{10}⟩,\\,s\\ge 0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3-8s}{10}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{6s+4}{10})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{8}{10},\\,\\frac{6}{10}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6c859aa-2556-59ff-a25e-6af1968d5cbe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6c859aa-2556-59ff-a25e-6af1968d5cbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c859aa-2556-59ff-a25e-6af1968d5cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" "answer-68140ba3-9983-541d-b347-0a33e474e0b6" "answer-3260ca78-14a6-50d0-b36b-a07da635b595" "answer-7429db73-b111-5e68-a8d3-3a5b83ea06db" "answer-1f54c52e-665b-579e-86df-670272b9e806"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" :answer/id #uuid "ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68140ba3-9983-541d-b347-0a33e474e0b6" :answer/id #uuid "68140ba3-9983-541d-b347-0a33e474e0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3260ca78-14a6-50d0-b36b-a07da635b595" :answer/id #uuid "3260ca78-14a6-50d0-b36b-a07da635b595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7429db73-b111-5e68-a8d3-3a5b83ea06db" :answer/id #uuid "7429db73-b111-5e68-a8d3-3a5b83ea06db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f54c52e-665b-579e-86df-670272b9e806" :answer/id #uuid "1f54c52e-665b-579e-86df-670272b9e806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e84a8d6-a1ed-5f78-832b-753ef57840b9" :question/id #uuid "8e84a8d6-a1ed-5f78-832b-753ef57840b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-83657" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,3-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩,\\,0\\le s<8\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{4}|\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92c3c624-d0ce-5d7e-af1f-33bffa533d5b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92c3c624-d0ce-5d7e-af1f-33bffa533d5b" :answer-field/id #uuid "92c3c624-d0ce-5d7e-af1f-33bffa533d5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482" :answer-field/choices ["answer-50a64c5e-ee2e-5e33-99cd-2507a3e15ed4" "answer-db8aafa7-86be-5335-ad0b-879f8daf56c3" "answer-df3fead8-a8d0-5dc8-8d4a-f1f7b93d5a94" "answer-e9f51edd-60f6-5c7d-8ca5-c07095020041" "answer-0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50a64c5e-ee2e-5e33-99cd-2507a3e15ed4" :answer/id #uuid "50a64c5e-ee2e-5e33-99cd-2507a3e15ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db8aafa7-86be-5335-ad0b-879f8daf56c3" :answer/id #uuid "db8aafa7-86be-5335-ad0b-879f8daf56c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df3fead8-a8d0-5dc8-8d4a-f1f7b93d5a94" :answer/id #uuid "df3fead8-a8d0-5dc8-8d4a-f1f7b93d5a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9f51edd-60f6-5c7d-8ca5-c07095020041" :answer/id #uuid "e9f51edd-60f6-5c7d-8ca5-c07095020041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482" :answer/id #uuid "0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-941975f4-ea50-5edb-a299-e8568f71e188" :question/id #uuid "941975f4-ea50-5edb-a299-e8568f71e188" :question/math-academy-id "q-83663" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\,-12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})i+12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3})\\,j,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}+{(12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12{t}^{2})^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+(12{t}^{2})^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12{t}^{2})^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3}))} \\\\  & =12{t}^{2} \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}+{(-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3{t}^{2})^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+(-3{t}^{2})^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3}))} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{12{t}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2ae9bf6-e514-5558-98b8-e081859740e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2ae9bf6-e514-5558-98b8-e081859740e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ae9bf6-e514-5558-98b8-e081859740e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac11b4df-2cb6-5f6b-92fb-3e07ba50cb5b" "answer-c2b8e622-9766-5512-823c-41c899359c51" "answer-4efce17f-3075-5e92-ad94-a11200baf0b2" "answer-8d0a7ca2-651b-528e-afe7-bc816f290417" "answer-3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac11b4df-2cb6-5f6b-92fb-3e07ba50cb5b" :answer/id #uuid "ac11b4df-2cb6-5f6b-92fb-3e07ba50cb5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2b8e622-9766-5512-823c-41c899359c51" :answer/id #uuid "c2b8e622-9766-5512-823c-41c899359c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4efce17f-3075-5e92-ad94-a11200baf0b2" :answer/id #uuid "4efce17f-3075-5e92-ad94-a11200baf0b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d0a7ca2-651b-528e-afe7-bc816f290417" :answer/id #uuid "8d0a7ca2-651b-528e-afe7-bc816f290417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99" :answer/id #uuid "3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121002 :tutorial/content "The **curvature** of a curve measures how much the curve \"bends\" at a given point. It can also be thought of as a measure of how much the curve deviates from being a straight line. Curvature is denoted by the Greek letter $\\kappa$ (pronounced \"kappa\"). \n\nIf $\\kappa=0$ at some point on a curve, then that curve looks like a straight line in some neighborhood of the point.\n\nIf the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ is parametrized by the arc length $s,$ then the curvature $\\kappa$ is the magnitude of the change of direction of the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T$ per unit of arc length. That is,\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\left\\| \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf T}{\\textrm{d}s}  \\right\\|= \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|.\n$$\n\nNote that $|| \\mathbf v ||$ denotes the magnitude of the vector $\\mathbf v.$\n\nFor example, suppose we are given the curve \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s)= \\left\\langle \\sin\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}, \\: -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \nwhich is parametrized by arc length $s.$ Let's find the curvature of  $\\mathbf r(s)$  at the point where $s={\\pi}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit tangent vector:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) =\\dfrac 12 \\left\\langle \\cos\\left( \\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\sqrt{3}, \\: \\sin \\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we differentiate $\\mathbf{T}(s)$ and evaluate its absolute value at $s=\\pi\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature by taking the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Note:** To calculate $\\kappa,$ the function $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ should be at least twice differentiable with respect to $s.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121007 :tutorial/content "If the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ is parametrized by a general parameter $t,$ then\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nTo understand why this is, remember that the arc length $s$ and the parameter $t$ are related by the formula \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle s(t)= \\int_0^t\\left\\| \\mathbf  r'(x)\\right\\|\\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nBy the chain rule and the fundamental theorem of calculus, then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\dfrac{\\textrm d  s}{\\textrm d t}= \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t)\\right\\|.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}‖ & =‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}s}‖‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =κ(t)‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ \\\\ κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120033 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
